    {
      "id": "claim_3c6e8649315f47ee8c2362e21a33b5af",
      "statement": "graceful: true has one meaning on both consumers - a step failure is recorded in the log and the database and the run continues with the next step - while the default aborts: the batch engine raises StepAbortError (carrying the failing step's PageState so it is still recorded), and the daemon runner gives non-graceful steps an attempt budget of 3 (MAX_STEP_ATTEMPTS, full chain re-executed) while graceful steps are single-attempt and never retried, then pauses the run instead of aborting on exhaustion.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/BillCollectorServices_pw.py#L367-L379",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a1d4fa156e0ccfa724ac02aca8f3818355dd5c3b2d767fc555490c06ed06ef4:"
