    {
      "id": "claim_90dd706eb2d54da886328d5aa96d9716",
      "statement": "helpers/BillCollectorCheckRecipe.py (CheckRecipe) is the run-time gate of both consumers - the batch path raises and the daemon runner exits 1 when it returns None for a missing or schema-invalid recipe - and as a CLI its __main__ block ignores the return value, so a schema violation is logged but exits 0; exit 1 occurs for a wrong argument count, a missing/unreadable/non-YAML schema file, a recipe without a usable $schema field (so a missing one-argument recipe file fails there), and a syntactically invalid recipe YAML in the explicit-schema form.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/BillCollectorServices_pw.py#L176-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee153436c02aafcd2da787c6a7fda145dd9c3c6a5d6661196f6eaf151cda4199:"
