    {
      "id": "claim_ebce4ca9c7ec46fdb384af937ff0bb58",
      "statement": "The UI recipe editor (/recipes/<service>) implements Save as validate -> atomic save -> optional git commit: when git_commit_enabled is truthy (default false) billcollector/gitcommit.git_commit stages exactly the recipe file (never git add -A) with the message recipe(<service>): <summary> (first changed service description, else edited via UI), treating a no-op save as success; opened with ?run=<run_id> it preloads a failure panel from the run's pause context and a candidate's Use button replaces the failed step's locator prefix via apply_candidate_to_step (which never mutates its input and refuses steps without a locator prefix or nested expect_download steps).",
